# Executables left at the repository root by `go build ./cmd/<name>`.
#
# Without an -o, go build writes the binary into the working directory named
# after the command's directory. Run from the root -- which is where every
# other go command here is run -- that leaves a multi-megabyte executable
# beside the source, untracked and easy to sweep into a `git add`. One such
# commit added five of them, 19 MB, and they reached a shared branch.
#
# THE FIRST ATTEMPT AT THIS RULE SAT DEAD IN THIS FILE FOR ITS ENTIRE LIFE:
# a missing newline joined this rule's ignore pattern to an unrelated entry
# above it, producing one path that matched nothing rather than two that
# matched something. It was split and repaired in 9c654f56. This list is the
# complete set of cmd/ names, kept in sync so a partial one never reads as
# an omission.
/action-gen
/generated-value-strip
/list-resource-gen
/metadata-contract-gen
/nested-custom-type-strip
/nested-type-dedup
/provider-spec-compiler
/schema-behaviour
/sdk-bootstrap

# provider-codegen's compiler intermediates. *.provider-code-spec.json is the
# hand-off between provider-spec-compiler and tfplugingen-framework/
# list-resource-gen/action-gen -- go generate writes and reads it within the
# same run, so it never needs to survive between them. *.impact.json is
# retired: nothing in this tree has emitted or read one for a while: the
# compiler's Result no longer has the field. Neither belongs in the diff a
# reviewer reads; *.mapping.json is not here because descriptor_mapping_test.go
# reads the committed copy directly, as its own independent record.
provider-codegen/generated/*.impact.json
*.provider-code-spec.json
